	(no_connect
		(at 337.82 332.74)
		(uuid "546f2bfd-61af-5308-819b-6d2e9d0e488b")
	)
	(text "G0B1VET6 pin plan: parts check 68 of 68 against ST pin data. Extra lines beyond the plan: PC2/PC3 buck off, PF0/PF1 PG, PF3-5 rail flags, PB9 EN_CLEAN3. PF10 was BOARD_PRESENT, now BANK_B_CLOSE. PC9 WD_KICK, PE15 FLT_A, PE0 ESTOP_ARMED, PE1 WD_N read-back, input only, 10k in series. PD8-11, PD15, PD2 are now PORT_REQ, gated in hardware to PORT_EN.\nI2C: 3 hardware buses. I2C1 HP meters, I2C2 AFE, I2C3 to TCA9546A at 0x70 (ch0 meters A, ch1 meters B, ch2 Qwiic, ch3 spare).\nFive NTC channels sit on 10k to the ADC reference. NTC_BOARD1 also reads open when the HP board is missing: replaces BOARD_PRESENT."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 254 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9d6d4b8e-a189-52e2-a74f-095858c1f54d")
	)
	(text "12 V LOAD SHED (budget sums to 22 A on a 12.5 A converter, DC limit 14.2 A min). U1321 meters the real total on +12V: amps are not summed across rails. Start values, tune on the bench.\n1. Above 10.5 A, 500 ms: fans to reduced duty (FANx_PWM).\n2. Above 11.0 A, 500 ms: third board off (EN_12V_THIRD).\n3. HARDWARE, above 12.0 A, about 150 us: U1321 ALERT latches SHED_N: third board, aux and spare off through 1k series FETs, no firmware. Firmware clears after the total stays under 10.5 A.\n4. Above 12.4 A for 1 s with step 3 done: Pi stub and Jetson last, after telling the host. PG_12V falling alone never sheds compute: log only.\nPORT SOFTWARE TRIP (firmware): each ADC_IMx, 1-15 A per port, default 15 A on arm and waist, 10 A on aux. Over the limit drops PORT_REQx, then reset needs the 148 ms latch sequence.\nWATCHDOG: kick WD_KICK from the main loop only, after the port and pack checks ran. 1.36-1.84 s, not firmware-startable or stoppable."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 270 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ab329f7d-d698-5569-a319-ef588a657f0d")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
